{"sections": [
  {"key": "arc", "title": "The arc", "sentences": [
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Revenue compounded 6.2% a year from $26.6 billion in FY2016 to $45.7 billion in FY2025 [F1][F10][F157], but the path was a cycle, not a straight line."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Revenue rose 25.6% in FY2018 to $37.4 billion [F3][D93], with the Wirtgen acquisition adding 12% to net sales that year [P72]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "The peak was FY2023 at $61.3 billion [F8], followed by declines of 15.6% in FY2024 and 11.7% in FY2025 [D367][D412]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "The FY2024 fall came from lower shipment volumes across every equipment segment, driven by rising grain stocks, lower commodity prices and elevated interest rates [P17]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "drivers", "title": "What drove growth", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Production Agriculture was the largest driver, at 37.1% of FY2025 revenue [D657], and it subtracted 7.0pp from growth that year [D659]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "Its FY2025 decline came as sales volumes fell 30% in the U.S. and Canada, partly offset by a 22% increase in Brazil [P10]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Construction & Forestry, 25.5% of revenue [D889], fell 11.8% and subtracted 3.0pp [D890][D891]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating income grew faster than revenue over the window, at a 16.9% CAGR against 6.2% [F159][F157], but incremental margin turned negative in FY2024 at 41.1% [D388]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Diluted EPS compounded 16.1% against net income's 14.2% [F162][F160], as the diluted share count fell 1.9% in FY2025 [D427]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "margins", "title": "Margins and costs", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating margin was 17.5% in FY2024 [F30], above the 12.1% window median but below the 21.2% FY2023 high [D1335][D1334]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "The FY2024 margin fell 3.7pp [D378], with SG&A costing 1.9pp and R&D 0.9pp [D391][D390]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "FY2024 production costs were favorable on lower material and profit-sharing costs, partly offset by higher overhead from lower volumes [P16]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Net margin fell 2.7pp to 11.0% in FY2025 [F50][D422], and the 20.1% effective tax rate was below the 22.7% of FY2024 [D400][D355]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Net margin sat 3.7pp below operating margin in FY2024 [D1373], reflecting interest expense of $3.3 billion [X81]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "cash", "title": "Cash conversion", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating cash flow of $7.5 billion was 1.48x net income in FY2025 [F80][F40][D401], above the 1.17x window median [D1364]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "The FY2025 inflow came from net income adjusted for non-cash provisions and a decrease in sales receivables, partly offset by an OPEB contribution [P5]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Free cash flow was $6.1 billion, a 13.4% margin [F100][D398], with capex at 3.0% of revenue and 0.61x D&A [D397][D403]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Free cash flow per dollar of net income was 1.21x [D402], in the 100th percentile against a 0.95x peer median [D1359][D1360]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "balance_sheet", "title": "Balance sheet and capital allocation", "sentences": [
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Cash was $8.3 billion at FY2025 [F140], up 13.0% [D420], against $13.8 billion of current debt [X185]."},
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Long-term debt is not reported after FY2021 [X191], so net cash and debt-based peer ranks cannot be computed across the window [R9]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Buybacks plus dividends of $2.9 billion were 46.9% of free cash flow in FY2025 [D409][D410], down from $8.6 billion and 121.9% in FY2023 [D319][D320]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Return on average equity fell to 20.6% [D411], in the 17th percentile against a 28.3% peer median [D1361][D1362]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "red_flags", "title": "Red flags", "sentences": [
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Revenue fell in both FY2024 and FY2025 [F9][F10], a two-year decline [R1]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "The FY2025 drop was concentrated in Production Agriculture, 37.1% of revenue and down 17.6% [D657][D658], on a 30% U.S. and Canada volume fall [P10]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "Small Agriculture & Turf operating profit fell on lower volumes and higher tariffs, partly offset by price realization [P8]."},
    {"type": "fact", "text": "The debt series breaks at FY2021, so net-cash and debt-growth comparisons across the window are unreliable [R9][X191]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "watch", "title": "What to watch", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Watch whether operating margin holds above the 12.1% window median [D1335] or falls toward the 9.7% FY2016 low [D1333], reported in the FY2026 10-K."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Watch Production Agriculture revenue against the FY2025 level of $17.0 billion [S254]; a further decline would extend the two-year slide [R1]."},
